=[ tomet-config ]

==[ tomet-config ]

Configuration parsing and styling rule definitions ([`Config`], [`FormatConfig`], [`MetaConfig`], [`WorkspaceConfig`]).

==[ Architecture & Responsibilities ]

- Centralized Configuration Domain:

`tomet-config` owns configuration data structures and pure parsing
([`load_config_from_str`]). Finding and reading a config file off
disk is `tomet-load-config`'s job, one layer up.

- Root Group Modules:
  - `groups` configuration groups ([`FormatConfig`], [`MetaConfig`], [`WorkspaceConfig`], [`MacrosConfig`], [`RegistryConfig`], [`ApiConfig`]).:Root
  - `discovery` parsing and error handling.:Configuration
  - `tree` tree normalization and path lookup utilities.:AST

==[ Module discovery ]

Config parsing and error reporting. Finding and reading a config file
off disk is `tomet-load-config`'s job, one layer up -- this stays
pure so `tomet-config` itself can stay layer 3 and disk-free.
[`ConfigError::Io`] exists for that crate's `load_config_from_file`
to construct; nothing in this crate ever produces it.

===[ Enums ]

====[ enum ConfigError ]

===[ Functions ]

====[ fn load_config_from_str ]

==[ Module groups ]

Root configuration groups corresponding to `@settings{ ... }` / `@config{ ... }` sections.

Each submodule defines a dedicated strongly-typed configuration struct for a specific domain:

- `format`, link, element, callout, list, and table formatting rules ([`FormatConfig`], [`GroupOrder`]).:Heading
- `meta` metadata formatting and schema rules ([`MetaConfig`], [`FieldConfig`]).:Document
- `workspace` file indexing exclusions and unswept rules ([`WorkspaceConfig`]).:Vault
- `macros` template expansions ([`MacrosConfig`]).:Macro
- `registry` and vocabularies declarations ([`RegistryConfig`]).:Blueprints
- `api` extraction settings ([`ApiConfig`]).:API

